cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use slipguard, TranscriptLab or the PNC corpus, please cite the paper below."
title: "slipguard: Stopping Gemma 4 Agents From Imitating Their Own Corrupted Tool Calls"
abstract: >-
  slipguard, a Gemma 4 tool-call hygiene library (strict parser with a vLLM plugin, history quarantine, an
  intent-preserving repair proxy, a patched chat template, transcript and checkpoint audits); TranscriptLab, a
  causal history-intervention benchmark with a CLI; and PNC, a public corpus of 1,181 Gemma 4 SWE-bench agent
  trajectories (41,290 model turns, 1,167 graded, 499 resolved).
version: 0.1.2
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aneeshm11/slipguard"
url: "https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cassinicraft/slipguard-pnc"
keywords: [tool calling, function calling, Gemma 4, agents, transcript hygiene, causal benchmark, parser conformance, dataset]
authors:
